Name     oe-always;
PartNo   00;
Date     2026-01-01;
Revision 01;
Designer decpld;
Company  decpld;
Assembly none;
Location none;
Device   g22v10;

/* SPEC.md 7.4, output enable: always enabled, stated explicitly.

   `in2` reaches the same state by saying nothing about the enable, so
   comparing the two answers a separate question: does an explicit
   `o0.oe = 'b'1` produce the same fuses as CUPL's own default, or does
   the compiler treat the two differently? A difference would mean the
   default is not what it appears to be. */

PIN 2  = i0;
PIN 23 = o0;

o0    = i0;
o0.oe = 'b'1;
